
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.GetLinkNumber(): number`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer llGetLinkNumber();`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns an integer that is the link number of the prim containing the script.</p>
  <p>`0` means the prim is not linked, `1` the prim is the root, `2` the prim is the first child, etc. Links are numbered in the reverse order in which they were linked -- if you select a box, a sphere and a cylinder in that order, then link them, the cylinder is 1, the sphere is 2 and the box is 3. The last selected prim has the lowest link number.</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>prim</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">139</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>By design may equal <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetNumberOfPrims" target="_blank">llGetNumberOfPrims</a>, <i>e.g.</i>, when prim is last, object contains multiple prims, and no sitting avatars</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    ll.OwnerSay(tostring(ll.GetLinkNumber()))
    ll.OwnerSay(tostring(ll.GetNumberOfPrims()))
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llOwnerSay((string) llGetLinkNumber());
        llOwnerSay((string) llGetNumberOfPrims());
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>A non-obvious feature is using double-negation to obtain a link number zero (for an unlinked prim) or one (for the root of a linkset). Unlike constants like <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LINK_ROOT" target="_blank">LINK_ROOT</a>, this number can be used directly with functions like <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetLinkPrimitiveParams" target="_blank">llGetLinkPrimitiveParams</a> without first determining whether a prim is part of a linkset:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local function main()
    local rootLinkNum = if ll.GetLinkNumber() == 0 then 0 else 1
    -- returns 0 in an unlinked prim, 1 in a linkset

    local isFullBright = ll.List2Integer(ll.GetLinkPrimitiveParams(rootLinkNum, {PRIM_FULLBRIGHT, ALL_SIDES}), 0)
-- TRUE if all sides of an unlinked prim or the root of a linkset are set to full bright, FALSE otherwise
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        integer rootLinkNum = !!llGetLinkNumber();
        // returns 0 in an unlinked prim, 1 in a linkset

        integer isFullBright = llList2Integer(llGetLinkPrimitiveParams(rootLinkNum,[PRIM_FULLBRIGHT, ALL_SIDES]),0);
        // TRUE if all sides of an unlinked prim or the root of a linkset are set to full bright, FALSE otherwise
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
